  "question": "What did ships carry from Muziris?",
  "question_lang": null,
  "answer": "According to the Periplus of the Erythraean Sea, ships carried pepper from Muziris, which \"is produced in quantity in only one region near these markets, a district called Cottonara.\" [S1] The text also lists other exports from Muziris: \"great quantities of fine pearls, ivory, silk cloth, spikenard from the Ganges, malabathrum from the places in the interior, transparent stones of all kinds, diamonds and sapphires, and tortoise-shell.\" [S1] A Tamil literary text from the Sangam period describes Yavana (Greek-Roman) vessels at Muciri \"arriving with gold and departing with pepper.\" [S5]",
